  "R0.73T 的 L4 压力机制、壳层强制性与 Wiener 邻近文献": "Literature near R0.73T on the L4 pressure mechanism, shell coercivity, and Wiener methods",
  "R0.73T 的主张边界": "Claim boundary for R0.73T",
  "R0.73U 的 KHM、精确 filtering 与带符号三阶通量邻近文献": "Literature adjacent to R0.73U on KHM, exact filtering, and signed third-order flux",
  "R0.73U 的主张边界": "Claim boundaries for R0.73U",
  "R0.73V 的精确 filtered-moment 层级与压力感知三阶界面": "R0.73V exact filtered-moment hierarchy and pressure-aware third-order interface",
  "R0.73V 的主张边界": "R0.73V claim boundary",
  "R0.73W 的带符号亚滤波 production 与 heat-plane 特征线边界": "R0.73W boundary for signed subfilter production and heat-plane characteristics",
  "R0.73W 的主张边界": "Claim boundary of R0.73W",
  "R0.73X 的 explicit exterior tails 与 positive-scale size 边界": "R0.73X explicit exterior tails and positive-scale size boundary",
  "R0.73X 的价值在于把一个含混的 local remainder 问题拆成可独立攻击的三层：direct Gaussian velocity/pressure-source transport、algebraic harmonic pressure tail，以及 signed payment 到 positive size 的 coercivity bridge。 第一层与第二层现在有 exact definitions、scale audit、positive-scale size proof 与 independent readback。这样，后续若提出更强 theorem，就不能再把 pressure nonlocality 或 zero-scale endpoint 隐藏在“lower-order error”里。 同样重要的是，本节关闭了两个精确定义的错误方向：fixed probe class 的 amplitude-independent quadratic absorption，以及没有 exterior input 的 velocity-only functional tail estimate。 仍未闭合的不是另一个 algebraic identity，而是式 (1.7)：怎样从 signed information 得到能进入 CKN/Koch--Tataru interface 的 positive smallness， 同时保留 compact cutoff、harmonic pressure 与 suitable-weak defect。 因此这一节是 rigorous boundary result，而不是 regularity theorem，更不是 Clay problem 的完成比例。": "The value of R0.73X is that it decomposes an ambiguous local remainder problem into three independently attackable layers: direct Gaussian velocity/pressure-source transport, an algebraic harmonic pressure tail, and a coercivity bridge from signed payment to positive size. The first and second layers now have exact definitions, a scale audit, a positive-scale size proof, and an independent readback. Any subsequent stronger theorem can therefore no longer hide pressure nonlocality or the zero-scale endpoint inside a “lower-order error.” Equally importantly, this section closes two precisely defined false directions: amplitude-independent quadratic absorption for a fixed probe class, and a velocity-only functional tail estimate with no exterior input. What remains unclosed is not another algebraic identity but equation (1.7): how to derive positive smallness suitable for the CKN/Koch--Tataru interface from signed information while retaining a compact cutoff, harmonic pressure, and a suitable-weak defect. This section is therefore a rigorous boundary result, not a regularity theorem and still less a completion percentage for the Clay problem.",
  "R0.73X 的主张边界": "Claim boundary for R0.73X",
