  "我按原编号记录推导、反例和未解决的问题。": "I record derivations, counterexamples, and unresolved questions under their original identifiers.",
  "这页接在 R0.00–R0.60 的阶段回顾之后，完整保留 R0.61 到 R0.72Y 的 115 个研究节点。R0.69P 以后的路线从局部证书推进到 scalar A2 collision path，再在 R0.72Y 回到完整 Fourier--Leray linearized row。scalar forced transfer 按 standard 与 semiclassical negative norms 分开闭合；exact lift-up 排除 epsilon-only full-row strict contraction。完整 low-gap vector row、nonlinear Navier--Stokes 与 Clay 都没有被外推。": "This page follows the phase recap for R0.00–R0.60 and fully retains the 115 research nodes from R0.61 through R0.72Y. After R0.69P, the route advances from local certificates to the scalar A2 collision path, then returns in R0.72Y to the complete Fourier--Leray linearized row. Scalar forced transfer closes separately for standard and semiclassical negative norms; exact lift-up rules out epsilon-only full-row strict contraction. The complete low-gap vector row, nonlinear Navier--Stokes, and Clay are not extrapolated.",
  "直接研究 \\(q\\to\\eta\\) 三角系统，按 orientation ratio、damping gap 和 exceptional rows 分区，并保留 lift-up transient prefactor。": "Study the \\(q\\to\\eta\\) triangular system directly, partition by orientation ratio, damping gap, and exceptional rows, and retain the lift-up transient prefactor.",
  "epsilonOnlyFullRowClosure、allPhysicalRowsUniformStrictContraction、standardHMinusOneTransferAlpha2 与 HMinusOneEndpointAlphaGain 为 FALSE；strongFullRowA2Estimate、completeLinearizedShearSubsystem、nonlinearNavierStokes 与 Clay 为 OPEN。": "epsilonOnlyFullRowClosure, allPhysicalRowsUniformStrictContraction, standardHMinusOneTransferAlpha2, and HMinusOneEndpointAlphaGain are FALSE; strongFullRowA2Estimate, completeLinearizedShearSubsystem, nonlinearNavierStokes, and Clay are OPEN.",
  "R0.00–R0.60 的内容保留在上一份阶段回顾中。R0.70A–R0.72Y 的 77 个版本已公开，其中 53 个满足当前 formal-figure 完整封存合同。公开和封存不表示 Clay 问题已经解决。": "The content from R0.00–R0.60 remains in the preceding phase recap. Seventy-seven versions from R0.70A–R0.72Y are public, and 53 satisfy the current complete formal-figure sealing contract. Publication and sealing do not mean that the Clay problem has been solved.",
