  "R0.70A–R0.73P 已公开版本": "Published Releases R0.70A–R0.73P",
  "R0.73P 的有限公式诊断和正式附图只作复现与错误探测；不认证 PDE 阈值必要性、非线性平滑、奇性或 Clay。NOT CLAY。": "The finite formula diagnostics and formal figures for R0.73P serve only reproducibility and error detection; they do not certify the necessity of a PDE threshold, nonlinear smoothing, singularity formation, or Clay. NOT CLAY.",
  "R0.73P 附图": "R0.73P Figures",
  "R0.73P 有限诊断包": "R0.73P Finite Diagnostics Package",
  "R0.73P 证明：固定先验全局强轨道具有正的临界 \\(H^{1/2}\\) 稳定管；带限扰动由 \\(N^{-1/2}\\) 的充分 \\(L^2\\) 门槛进入该管。每条弱分支晚时与固定强轨道同步，但无频率条件的早期强正则仍开放。": "R0.73P proves that a fixed a priori global strong orbit has a positive critical \\(H^{1/2}\\) stability tube; band-limited perturbations enter that tube through the sufficient \\(N^{-1/2}\\) \\(L^2\\) gate. Every weak branch synchronizes with the fixed strong orbit at late times, but early strong regularity without a frequency condition remains open.",
  "R0.73Q：检查 L2-only / 高频输入接口": "R0.73Q: Examine the L2-only / High-Frequency Input Interface",
  "01 · 52 个研究阶段": "01 · 52 research phases",
  "02 · 133 节完整索引": "02 · Complete 133-section index",
  "52 个阶段、133 个节点：从约化递推和环带排除到临界热流稳定管与端点边界。": "52 phases and 133 nodes: from reduced recurrences and annular exclusion to a critical heat-flow stability tube and endpoint boundaries.",
  "保留 R0.73P 历史回顾": "Retain the R0.73P historical recap",
  "本页保留 R0.61 到 R0.73Q 的全部 133 个节点。R0.61–R0.69W 从约化递推走到严格环带排除；R0.70A–R0.71Z 检查移动尺度、临界账本、内部 entry 与 complete-root 边界；R0.72A–R0.73B 处理 strong coupling、critical log、碰撞几何与完整线性 Fourier--Leray 行；R0.73C–I 依次处理冻结 Rayleigh 不稳定、黏性谱簇持续、固定正半平面传递、移动剖面增益、非线性相对放大、平面固定距离偏离与零窗口作用量边界。R0.73J 认证无黏连续谱支，R0.73K 闭合参数一致的黏性 rank-one 谱支，R0.73L 把冻结谱支升级为真实非自治 selected action；R0.73M 再用完整 action 指定种子，并在固定物理时刻闭合二维非线性固定距离偏离。背景随 \\(\\Lambda\\) 改变，轨道留在精确二维不变子空间；prefactor 极限、两项 WKB、固定背景、横向三维、奇性与 Clay 没有被外推。 R0.73M 证明：当 \\(\\Lambda\\to\\infty\\) 且背景随之改变时，按完整作用量 缩小的平面扰动可以在固定时刻保持固定阶输出。R0.73N 补上固定成员审计： 任意共存强解满足有限累积应变控制；平面扰动全局满足 \\(L^2\\) 稳定估计； 足够小的全三维 \\(H^3\\) 扰动落在正的全局强解稳定管内。因此，R0.73M 中的量词顺序不能交换为一个固定背景上的任意小输入、固定距离逃逸。 R0.73O 关闭了已知全局无强迫背景上的 \\(H^3\\)-小扰动不稳定路线：每条轨道最终衰减，累积 \\(H^4\\) 作用量有限，并有一个对所有起始时刻有效的正稳定半径。强迫对照保留无限累积应变，并由平面方向给出全局光滑、初始 \\(H^3\\) 趋零而输出固定 \\(L^2\\) 逃逸的见证。 R0.73P 关闭了固定全局强轨道周围的临界稳定与带限输入接口：临界管对所有起始时刻有效，\\(N^{-1/2}\\) 指数对范数转移精确，并允许 \\(L^2\\) 趋零而 \\(H^3\\) 发散的光滑扰动。能量球内所有弱分支在共同延迟后正则并相对参考轨道同步；不能跨越的部分是此前的早期弱区间。 这一节用周期 Stokes--HLS 双线性估计和有限 Volterra 递推，构造了一个全起点统一的临界热流稳定管。精确 Fourier 族证明它加入了旧 \\(H^{1/2}\\) 管之外的光滑安全数据；裸 Kato 上确界则被一个时间端点反例阻断。whole-space Besov 开放性属于已知文献，Clay 结论仍开放。": "This page retains all nodes from R0.61 through R0.73Q, 133 in total. R0.61–R0.69W moves from reduced recurrences to rigorous annular exclusion; R0.70A–R0.71Z examines moving scales, the critical ledger, internal entry, and the complete-root boundary; R0.72A–R0.73B treats strong coupling, the critical log, collision geometry, and the complete linear Fourier--Leray row; R0.73C–I successively treats frozen Rayleigh instability, persistence of viscous spectral clusters, transfer to a fixed positive half-plane, moving-profile gain, nonlinear relative amplification, fixed-distance planar departure, and the zero-window action boundary. R0.73J certifies the inviscid spectral branch of the continuum operator; R0.73K closes the parameter-uniform viscous rank-one spectral branch; and R0.73L upgrades the frozen spectral branch to a genuine nonautonomous selected action. R0.73M then specifies the seed through the full action and closes two-dimensional nonlinear fixed-distance departure at a fixed physical time. The background varies with \\(\\Lambda\\), while the orbit stays in the exact two-dimensional invariant subspace; the prefactor limit, two-term WKB, a fixed background, transverse three-dimensional effects, singularity, and Clay are not extrapolated. R0.73M proves that, as \\(\\Lambda\\to\\infty\\) with the background varying accordingly, planar perturbations scaled down by the full action can retain fixed-order output at a fixed time. R0.73N adds the fixed-member audit: every coexisting strong solution obeys finite accumulated-strain control; planar perturbations satisfy a global \\(L^2\\) stability estimate; and sufficiently small fully three-dimensional \\(H^3\\) perturbations lie in a positive global strong-solution stability tube. Hence the quantifier order in R0.73M cannot be exchanged for arbitrarily small inputs escaping to a fixed distance on one fixed background. R0.73O closes the \\(H^3\\)-small perturbation instability route around known global unforced backgrounds: every orbit eventually decays, has finite accumulated \\(H^4\\) action, and possesses a positive stability radius valid at every initial time. The forced comparison retains infinite accumulated strain and supplies a globally smooth planar witness whose initial \\(H^3\\) norm tends to zero while its output escapes by a fixed \\(L^2\\) distance. R0.73P closes the critical stability and band-limited input interfaces around a fixed global strong orbit: the critical tube is valid at every initial time, the \\(N^{-1/2}\\) exponent is exact for norm transfer, and smooth perturbations may tend to zero in \\(L^2\\) while diverging in \\(H^3\\). Every weak branch in the energy ball becomes regular after a common delay and synchronizes relative to the reference orbit; the uncrossed part is the preceding early weak interval. This section uses a periodic Stokes--HLS bilinear estimate and finite Volterra recursion to construct a critical heat-flow stability tube uniform over all starting times. An exact Fourier family proves that it adds smooth safe data outside the old \\(H^{1/2}\\) tube; a time-endpoint counterexample blocks the bare Kato supremum. Whole-space Besov openness belongs to the established literature, and the Clay conclusion remains open.",
  "不能把 133 个节点或 95 个公开版本解释成 Clay 完成比例。单模与时间反例只认证公式和一条失败路线，不覆盖任意 L2-small 数据。有限时奇性和任意初值全局正则性仍为 OPEN。": "Neither the 133 nodes nor the 95 public releases can be interpreted as a percentage of Clay completion. The single-mode and time counterexamples certify only formulas and one failed route; they do not cover arbitrary L2-small data. Finite-time singularity and global regularity for arbitrary initial data remain OPEN.",
