  "54 个阶段、135 个节点：从约化递推和环带排除到二次自相关证书、尖锐差集障碍与低摘要不可辨识性。": "54 stages and 135 nodes: from reduced recurrences and annular exclusion to a quadratic autocorrelation certificate, a sharp difference-set obstruction, and low-summary non-identifiability.",
  "保留 R0.73R 历史回顾": "Keep the R0.73R historical recap",
  "本页保留 R0.61 到 R0.73S 的全部 135 个节点。R0.61–R0.69W 从约化递推走到严格环带排除；R0.70A–R0.71Z 检查移动尺度、临界账本、内部 entry 与 complete-root 边界；R0.72A–R0.73B 处理 strong coupling、critical log、碰撞几何与完整线性 Fourier--Leray 行；R0.73C–I 依次处理冻结 Rayleigh 不稳定、黏性谱簇持续、固定正半平面传递、移动剖面增益、非线性相对放大、平面固定距离偏离与零窗口作用量边界。R0.73J 认证无黏连续谱支，R0.73K 闭合参数一致的黏性 rank-one 谱支，R0.73L 把冻结谱支升级为真实非自治 selected action；R0.73M 再用完整 action 指定种子，并在固定物理时刻闭合二维非线性固定距离偏离。背景随 \\(\\Lambda\\) 改变，轨道留在精确二维不变子空间；prefactor 极限、两项 WKB、固定背景、横向三维、奇性与 Clay 没有被外推。 R0.73M 证明：当 \\(\\Lambda\\to\\infty\\) 且背景随之改变时，按完整作用量 缩小的平面扰动可以在固定时刻保持固定阶输出。R0.73N 补上固定成员审计： 任意共存强解满足有限累积应变控制；平面扰动全局满足 \\(L^2\\) 稳定估计； 足够小的全三维 \\(H^3\\) 扰动落在正的全局强解稳定管内。因此，R0.73M 中的量词顺序不能交换为一个固定背景上的任意小输入、固定距离逃逸。 R0.73O 关闭了已知全局无强迫背景上的 \\(H^3\\)-小扰动不稳定路线：每条轨道最终衰减，累积 \\(H^4\\) 作用量有限，并有一个对所有起始时刻有效的正稳定半径。强迫对照保留无限累积应变，并由平面方向给出全局光滑、初始 \\(H^3\\) 趋零而输出固定 \\(L^2\\) 逃逸的见证。 R0.73P 关闭了固定全局强轨道周围的临界稳定与带限输入接口：临界管对所有起始时刻有效，\\(N^{-1/2}\\) 指数对范数转移精确，并允许 \\(L^2\\) 趋零而 \\(H^3\\) 发散的光滑扰动。能量球内所有弱分支在共同延迟后正则并相对参考轨道同步；不能跨越的部分是此前的早期弱区间。 这一节用周期 Stokes--HLS 双线性估计和有限 Volterra 递推，构造了一个全起点统一的临界热流稳定管。精确 Fourier 族证明它加入了旧 \\(H^{1/2}\\) 管之外的光滑安全数据；裸 Kato 上确界则被一个时间端点反例阻断。whole-space Besov 开放性属于已知文献，Clay 结论仍开放。 我把 R0.73R 的当前价值评为“可靠的桥接引理与反例工具”，而不是高水平正则性主定理。可保留之处是：分层拆开能量、加法几何与高阶相位；给出有限 Fourier 数据可复算的严格证书；用同谱确定性族证明二次能谱不足。 本节真正完成的是三件较窄但可用的工作。": "This page retains the nodes from R0.61 through R0.73S, all 135 of them. R0.61–R0.69W progressed from reduced recurrences to rigorous annular exclusion; R0.70A–R0.71Z examined moving scales, the critical ledger, the internal entry, and the complete-root boundary; R0.72A–R0.73B treated strong coupling, the critical log, collision geometry, and the complete linear Fourier--Leray row; R0.73C–I successively treated frozen Rayleigh instability, persistence of viscous spectral clusters, transfer in a fixed positive half-plane, gain for moving profiles, nonlinear relative amplification, fixed-distance planar departure, and the zero-window action boundary. R0.73J certified an inviscid continuous spectral branch, R0.73K closed a parameter-consistent viscous rank-one spectral branch, and R0.73L upgraded the frozen spectral branch to a genuine nonautonomous selected action; R0.73M then used the full action to specify the seed and closed a two-dimensional nonlinear fixed-distance departure at a fixed physical time. The background changes with \\(\\Lambda\\), while the trajectory stays in an exact two-dimensional invariant subspace; no extrapolation is made to a prefactor limit, a two-term WKB expansion, a fixed background, transverse three-dimensional perturbations, singularity, or Clay. R0.73M proves that, as \\(\\Lambda\\to\\infty\\) with the background changing accordingly, planar perturbations scaled down by the full action can retain an output of fixed order at a fixed time. R0.73N adds the fixed-member audit: every coexisting strong solution obeys finite accumulated-strain control; planar perturbations satisfy a global \\(L^2\\) stability estimate; and sufficiently small fully three-dimensional \\(H^3\\) perturbations lie in a positive global strong-solution stability tube. Therefore, the quantifier order in R0.73M cannot be exchanged for arbitrarily small inputs escaping a fixed distance on one fixed background. R0.73O closes the \\(H^3\\)-small perturbative instability route around a known unforced global background: every trajectory eventually decays, the accumulated \\(H^4\\) action is finite, and a positive stability radius is valid for every starting time. The forced comparison retains infinite accumulated strain and, through a planar direction, supplies a globally smooth witness whose initial \\(H^3\\) norm tends to zero while its output exhibits a fixed \\(L^2\\) escape. R0.73P closes the critical-stability and band-limited input interfaces around a fixed global strong trajectory: the critical tube is valid for every starting time, the \\(N^{-1/2}\\) exponent is exact for norm transfer, and smooth perturbations may have vanishing \\(L^2\\) norm while their \\(H^3\\) norm diverges. Every weak branch in the energy ball regularizes after a common delay and synchronizes relative to the reference trajectory; the part that cannot be crossed is the earlier weak interval. This section constructs a critical heat-flow stability tube uniform over all starting times by using the periodic Stokes--HLS bilinear estimate and a finite Volterra recurrence. An exact Fourier family proves that it admits smooth safe data outside the old \\(H^{1/2}\\) tube; the bare Kato supremum is blocked by a time-endpoint counterexample. whole-space Besov openness belongs to the known literature, and the Clay conclusion remains open. I assess the current value of R0.73R as a reliable bridging lemma and counterexample tool, not a high-level regularity theorem. What should be retained is the layered separation of energy, additive geometry, and higher-order phase; a rigorous certificate that can be recomputed from finite Fourier data; and an isospectral deterministic family proving that quadratic energy spectra are insufficient. This section actually completes three narrower but usable tasks.",
  "不能把 135 个节点或 97 个公开版本解释成 Clay 完成比例。完整有限自相关确实决定六次矩；被否定的是预先声明的严格子集或低阶摘要。任意三维初值全局正则性仍为 OPEN。": "Neither the 135 nodes nor the 97 public versions can be interpreted as a percentage of Clay completion. The complete finite autocorrelation does determine the sixth moment; what is ruled out is a predeclared strict subset or a low-order summary. Global regularity for arbitrary three-dimensional initial data remains OPEN.",
